1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,646
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:29,988
[reporter] <i>More than a thousand</i>
<i>guns, including rifles</i>

6
00:00:30,071 --> 00:00:32,657
<i>and other firearms amounting</i>
<i>to over 50 million pesos,</i>

7
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:34,659
<i>are currently in police custody</i>
<i>after being seized</i>

8
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:37,287
<i>from a shipment made by Red Dragon.</i>

9
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:39,164
[Raul] <i>Why did you wear that mask?</i>

10
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:43,293
[Diego] <i>I'll do whatever it takes</i>
<i>to stop Red Dragon.</i>

11
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:47,756
<i>I'm telling you,</i>
<i>I didn't sabotage the shipment.</i>

12
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:49,007
<i>Then who did it?!</i>

13
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:53,928
<i>An impostor who goes around</i>
<i>and calls himself Jaguar.</i>

14
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:58,266
[Lily] <i>I have eyes watching you</i>
<i>even when I'm away.</i>

15
00:00:58,349 --> 00:00:59,768
<i>So, don't you ever dare.</i>

16
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:01,770
[Emilia] <i>Mama, that's my husband, Raul.</i>

17
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:04,856
<i>-Well, what do you do?</i>
<i>-I run a small jewelry business.</i>

18
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:08,443
<i>I didn't know you had</i>
<i>a thing for peasants.</i>

19
00:01:08,526 --> 00:01:10,153
<i>It's an anonymous text, Mom.</i>

20
00:01:11,237 --> 00:01:14,657
<i>It says they have proof that</i>
<i>Helena Montoya is Red Dragon.</i>

21
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:16,409
<i>This could be a trap.</i>

22
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:18,953
<i>I'm sorry, Mom, but I'm willing</i>
<i>to take that risk.</i>

23
00:01:19,037 --> 00:01:21,748
<i>And that's because I'm done</i>
<i>playing games with Red Dragon.</i>

24
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:23,792
<i>I've lost my patience.</i>

25
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:26,002
[Damian] <i>Raul couldn't have done it.</i>

26
00:01:26,085 --> 00:01:28,671
<i>The last time I saw him,</i>
<i>he was shot in the stomach.</i>

27
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:32,801
<i>But the man on the CCTV footage</i>
<i>didn't look like he was injured.</i>

28
00:01:32,884 --> 00:01:35,178
<i>Diego's pretending to be Jaguar.</i>

29
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:38,765
[Diego] <i>I'm taking you on your last ride!</i>

30
00:01:38,848 --> 00:01:42,519
<i>You'll never be the governor</i>
<i>of this province while I'm alive.</i>

31
00:01:50,819 --> 00:01:53,446
[pensive music playing]

32
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:56,533
[exhales]

33
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:00,995
Damn it.

34
00:02:21,474 --> 00:02:23,643
My mama burned you so bad.

35
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:28,398
What's with her anyway?
Is she really a philanthropist?

36
00:02:28,481 --> 00:02:29,899
Why does she talk like that?

37
00:02:31,025 --> 00:02:33,444
She's like a fire-breathing dragon!

38
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:51,045
[Natalie yelps]

39
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:52,463
<i>-Who are you?!</i>
<i>-Madrigal!</i>

40
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:54,757
[Natalie] <i>Aren't you happy to see me?</i>

41
00:02:54,841 --> 00:02:57,051
<i>I thought you liked me.</i>

42
00:02:58,970 --> 00:02:59,888
<i>What do you want, really?</i>

43
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:01,973
[Jepoy] <i>Why did you save me from Jaguar?</i>

44
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:03,975
<i>I want you to work for me.</i>

45
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:05,393
[Jepoy] <i>What do you want me to do?</i>

46
00:03:05,476 --> 00:03:07,896
[Natalie] <i>Can you make me happy?</i>

47
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:09,731
<i>I have what you need.</i>

48
00:03:09,814 --> 00:03:13,359
<i>And you have exactly what I want.</i>

49
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:16,321
<i>-You're lucky I found you.</i>
<i>-I knew you'd save me.</i>

50
00:03:16,404 --> 00:03:17,488
[Jepoy] <i>Be careful next time.</i>

51
00:03:17,572 --> 00:03:19,115
<i>I don't want this happening again.</i>

52
00:03:19,198 --> 00:03:22,327
[Natalie] <i>You have feelings for Madrigal.</i>

53
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:25,538
<i>Could he actually love me? How?</i>

54
00:03:26,664 --> 00:03:29,918
<i>Through Lily.</i>

55
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:31,711
<i>I want to make a proposal.</i>

56
00:03:31,794 --> 00:03:35,173
<i>I want to help Lily.</i>

57
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:39,427
<i>Lily Cruz refused my help? Is she insane?</i>

58
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:43,765
<i>Who exactly is stopping me from</i>
<i>joining forces with Lily Cruz?</i>

59
00:03:43,848 --> 00:03:46,059
<i>-It's Anna.</i>
<i>-What?</i>

60
00:03:51,105 --> 00:03:53,233
I want you, Madrigal.

61
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:59,239
And I know that I'll have you.

62
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:08,331
Even if it means that I need
to swallow my pride…

63
00:04:09,499 --> 00:04:13,044
and bow down to Lily Cruz.

64
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:17,298
I'll do it.

65
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:20,760
For you.

66
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:26,307
[birds chirping]

67
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:31,104
I'm fine, Emilia.
I am as strong as a horse.

68
00:04:31,187 --> 00:04:34,190
Diego has always had it in for you.

69
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:36,234
And right now,
he's poisoning Arnaldo's mind.

70
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:37,860
So, why don't you do the same?

71
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:40,655
And look how that turned out?

72
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:45,034
The black sheep is still alive.

73
00:04:46,035 --> 00:04:47,161
So, please.

74
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:52,750
Don't chastise an old man
who's got a bomb ticker.

75
00:04:53,876 --> 00:04:57,839
Papa, Diego said he'd do
everything to prevent

76
00:04:57,922 --> 00:04:59,799
your return to office.

77
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,051
Why am I telling you this?

78
00:05:02,135 --> 00:05:05,763
Unlike Mama, all you ever do
is talk down on me.

79
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:07,682
But I still care for you no matter what.

80
00:05:07,765 --> 00:05:11,185
So, in times like these,
we need to team up.

81
00:05:12,061 --> 00:05:13,730
We will, Emilia.

82
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:17,400
But you do not tell me what to do.

83
00:05:18,192 --> 00:05:23,489
If Diego dies, I want to make
sure it's my call,

84
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,200
and that I'll leave no trace.

85
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:31,789
[sighs]

86
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,546
[tense music playing]

87
00:05:38,921 --> 00:05:40,089
[door opens]

88
00:05:43,843 --> 00:05:44,844
See you later, Mom.

89
00:05:54,812 --> 00:05:57,523
[tense music continues]

90
00:06:00,568 --> 00:06:02,737
Lily? What's wrong?

91
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:13,372
[tense music swells]

92
00:06:25,718 --> 00:06:26,969
What's the matter?

93
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:29,764
I feel like someone's watching us.

94
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:31,891
Watching our every move.

95
00:06:33,935 --> 00:06:35,812
Let's go. Get in the car.

96
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:37,730
Stay safe, Mom. Please go inside.

97
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:39,440
All right. Be careful, you two.

98
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:40,525
We will.

99
00:06:42,568 --> 00:06:45,029
[tense music continues]

100
00:06:45,905 --> 00:06:46,948
[car door opens]

101
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:50,368
Why are you here watching over Lily?

102
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:52,995
Didn't I tell you to stop bothering us?

103
00:06:54,038 --> 00:06:55,706
Don't you have anything else to do?

104
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:00,503
Weren't you listening to me the other day?

105
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:06,551
I told you, I was gonna offer
my help to Lily Cruz.

106
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:08,344
Are you, really?

107
00:07:08,427 --> 00:07:10,847
What will you get from helping Lily Cruz?

108
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:12,974
Why don't you just stop bugging us?

109
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:16,310
Do you think it's that easy?

110
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:19,272
I didn't save your life for nothing!

111
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:26,195
I wasn't having sex with you
for no reason.

112
00:07:27,321 --> 00:07:31,117
What kind of woman
do you think I am, huh?!

113
00:07:34,328 --> 00:07:40,376
I wanted to help Lily because I'm hoping…

114
00:07:41,502 --> 00:07:43,713
that… [sobs]

115
00:07:45,506 --> 00:07:50,928
that you'd see something good in me.

116
00:07:51,012 --> 00:07:53,097
[somber music playing]

117
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:59,103
I was hoping you would like me back.

118
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:03,149
[Natalie sobs]

119
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:11,574
Ma'am…

120
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:12,909
No.

121
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:17,163
It meant nothing, right?

122
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:21,042
What?

123
00:08:23,377 --> 00:08:24,670
What did you say?

124
00:08:29,467 --> 00:08:33,304
I should've known. Just leave my car.

125
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:37,016
Get out of my car, Madrigal.

126
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:41,103
-[whispers] Ma'am…
-I said, get out!

127
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:44,607
Get out! [sobs]

128
00:08:45,441 --> 00:08:47,735
[sobs]

129
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:50,446
Just go!

130
00:08:52,865 --> 00:08:55,159
[cries]

131
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,119
No!

132
00:08:59,622 --> 00:09:00,623
[bawls]

133
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:06,671
No doubt the Ardientes will
try to have you killed again.

134
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:08,464
[birds chirping]

135
00:09:08,714 --> 00:09:09,882
I'm not backing down.

136
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:12,718
And he will never get back in power again.

137
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:13,970
I just…

138
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:15,096
I wish I had prevented him

139
00:09:15,179 --> 00:09:16,639
from cheating in the first place.

140
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:21,018
Diego, we did everything for you to win.

141
00:09:21,435 --> 00:09:23,563
You did your part,
and so did the rest of us.

142
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:26,732
Don't ever regret doing the right thing

143
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:28,276
just because you didn't win.

144
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:32,238
I will keep fighting for you
and everyone else…

145
00:09:32,863 --> 00:09:34,782
who suffers for justice like you do.

146
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:37,159
[romantic music playing]

147
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:39,662
And it's because of people like you…

148
00:09:40,871 --> 00:09:42,331
that I find the courage to go on.

149
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:50,464
I've been wanting to give you this.

150
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:54,176
[romantic music continues]

151
00:09:57,388 --> 00:09:58,514
This is for you.

152
00:10:15,573 --> 00:10:16,824
It looks great on you.

153
00:10:18,409 --> 00:10:20,077
Thanks for everything, Diego.

154
00:10:31,922 --> 00:10:33,466
I love you so much.

155
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:52,693
Come on.

156
00:10:56,572 --> 00:10:59,116
[bawling]

157
00:11:01,285 --> 00:11:04,372
[suspenseful music playing]

158
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:06,624
Face it, Natalie.

159
00:11:06,707 --> 00:11:08,584
[whimpers]

160
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:10,378
He doesn't love you.

161
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:15,007
He will never love you.

162
00:11:16,884 --> 00:11:18,969
He will never love you!

163
00:11:23,182 --> 00:11:25,893
No one will ever love you!

164
00:11:25,976 --> 00:11:28,354
[bawls]

165
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:36,821
No one will love you, Natalie.
Can't you see?

166
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:39,949
[Natalie] <i>Arnaldo.</i>

167
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,077
<i>He didn't love you.</i>

168
00:11:43,869 --> 00:11:44,995
Raul…

169
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:47,998
[Natalie] <i>He just used you!</i>

170
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:50,292
<i>And he chose</i>

171
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:51,710
Emilia.

172
00:11:54,338 --> 00:11:55,673
And Madrigal?

173
00:11:59,468 --> 00:12:01,971
[screams]

174
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:03,973
No!

175
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:15,943
I'm done sleeping with men…

176
00:12:19,071 --> 00:12:22,825
who don't want to give me their love.

177
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:27,913
You… You even tried to coexist

178
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:32,042
with pathetic losers!

179
00:12:35,212 --> 00:12:36,881
What were you thinking?

180
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:43,095
[suspenseful music swells]

181
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:44,763
I will come back.

182
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:50,102
And I will recuperate.

183
00:12:53,022 --> 00:12:57,860
And when I do,
I'll come back with a vengeance!

184
00:13:19,715 --> 00:13:22,635
WHERE ARE YOU?

185
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:33,896
Why do I keep thinking about you, Jepoy?

186
00:13:34,563 --> 00:13:36,440
Why am I worried about you?

187
00:13:37,441 --> 00:13:43,113
Shouldn't I be mad at you
for going with that woman?

188
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:46,283
I hate this!
Why am I even feeling this way?

189
00:13:55,459 --> 00:13:56,460
Anna?

190
00:13:56,961 --> 00:13:59,296
[romantic music playing]

191
00:13:59,672 --> 00:14:01,131
Hey, hey, hey. Wait.

192
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:03,884
Let's talk-- Where are you going?

193
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:05,511
You're not going anywhere.
We need to talk.

194
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:09,098
Listen. You don't have to talk.
Just hear me out.

195
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:18,941
My deal with Natalie, about Lily?

196
00:14:20,025 --> 00:14:23,946
It's all over. We're not going
to go through with it.

197
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:30,703
So? Are you happy now?

198
00:14:32,788 --> 00:14:33,956
No.

199
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:36,333
What else do you want?

200
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:39,545
I did that for you, Anna.

201
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:42,006
Natalie won't bother Lily
anymore now that I called

202
00:14:42,089 --> 00:14:43,465
the deal off with her. Problem solved.

203
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:45,217
What about you?

204
00:14:46,468 --> 00:14:48,137
What if she tries to get you back?

205
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:52,558
[romantic music continues]

206
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:59,189
Do you know why I didn't
want you to make that deal?

207
00:15:00,441 --> 00:15:03,068
Because I don't want to see you together.

208
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:07,615
Because, Jepoy…

209
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:12,036
I don't think I can take it.

210
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:16,332
What do you mean?

211
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:20,711
-[whimpers]
-Why not?

212
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:23,172
Ouch! What's wrong?

213
00:15:23,255 --> 00:15:25,090
That hurts, Anna. Tell me. What's wrong?

214
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:26,842
Isn't it obvious?!

215
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:31,680
Jepoy, I like you.

216
00:15:32,514 --> 00:15:34,892
[romantic music swells]

217
00:15:35,517 --> 00:15:37,061
I like you.

218
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:55,496
Jepoy, I tried to deny
my feelings for you.

219
00:15:56,956 --> 00:16:00,501
I tried turning my attention to Diego…

220
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,879
because I'd rather love someone else…

221
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:08,425
than see you keep your hopes up for Lily.

222
00:16:12,721 --> 00:16:16,684
If you truly love Lily,
I'd accept that, Jepoy.

223
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:18,394
I'd be okay with it.

224
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:21,021
But you know what hurts?

225
00:16:22,147 --> 00:16:24,358
It's to see you and Natalie together!

226
00:16:24,441 --> 00:16:26,235
That's just not fair!

227
00:16:26,318 --> 00:16:28,779
Because I've always been here
for you, Jepoy!

228
00:16:28,862 --> 00:16:30,781
-Anna…
-I'm just here, waiting.

229
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:34,827
-Why her? Why, Jepoy?
-Don't cry. [shushes]

230
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:38,872
-Don't cry. It's okay.
-[cries]

231
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:48,298
Anna, there's nothing
between me and Natalie.

232
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:50,009
That's the truth.

233
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:53,262
I promise.

234
00:17:03,188 --> 00:17:04,898
I'm sorry, Jepoy.

235
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:10,029
Maybe I just needed to let this all out.

236
00:17:11,071 --> 00:17:14,575
I hope nothing changes between
us because of what I said.

237
00:17:15,617 --> 00:17:17,619
-I'm really sorry.
-Anna, wait! Anna!

238
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:33,594
[Anna exhales, sniffles]

239
00:17:36,346 --> 00:17:37,347
Anna.

240
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:40,184
What's wrong?

241
00:17:48,525 --> 00:17:49,526
Anna.

242
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,071
[Jepoy] Anna!

243
00:17:55,741 --> 00:17:56,825
[Arnaldo] Jepoy.

244
00:17:58,702 --> 00:18:00,079
What did you do to Anna?

245
00:18:07,294 --> 00:18:08,420
Jepoy…

246
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:11,173
[Diego] Careful, okay?

247
00:18:12,716 --> 00:18:14,426
I should've worn flats today, Diego.

248
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:16,011
[Ivy and Diego chuckle]

249
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:22,810
[dramatic music playing]

250
00:18:28,315 --> 00:18:30,567
Wait here. I'll just go check on Arnaldo.

251
00:18:30,984 --> 00:18:35,781
[dramatic music continues]

252
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:11,400
[tense music playing]

253
00:19:32,045 --> 00:19:33,172
[phone chimes]

254
00:19:35,507 --> 00:19:38,760
LET'S MEET AT
PACIFIC RESTAURANT NOW.

255
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:50,272
[Diego] Arnaldo's not there.
Maybe he went out with Anna.

256
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:57,070
The anonymous tipster texted me again.

257
00:19:57,946 --> 00:19:59,031
Are you going?

258
00:20:00,574 --> 00:20:03,785
In times like these, Diego,
I need to take risks…

259
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,247
so I can find the evidence I need.

260
00:20:08,207 --> 00:20:09,541
Promise me you'll stay safe,

261
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:12,461
and make sure you meet in a public place.

262
00:20:12,836 --> 00:20:14,338
If you want, I can come with you.

263
00:20:14,421 --> 00:20:17,591
No, it's okay. I can handle this myself.

264
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:18,884
Let's go then.

265
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:20,135
-I'll help you back.
-Okay.

266
00:20:20,594 --> 00:20:21,970
-Oh!
-Careful.

267
00:20:23,138 --> 00:20:24,806
[eerie music]

268
00:20:25,307 --> 00:20:26,558
I'm all right.

269
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:31,647
[tense music playing]

270
00:20:37,861 --> 00:20:39,071
Watch your step.

271
00:21:16,024 --> 00:21:17,025
Good evening, ma'am.

272
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:19,736
-Have you secured the area?
-Yes, ma'am.

273
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:20,946
The area is secured.

274
00:21:21,029 --> 00:21:22,030
Thank you.

275
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:30,414
Where are they?

276
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:31,790
Over there.

277
00:21:34,042 --> 00:21:35,043
Thank you.

278
00:21:36,878 --> 00:21:41,133
[suspenseful music playing]

279
00:21:50,934 --> 00:21:54,104
[laughing]

280
00:21:54,396 --> 00:21:56,940
-You?
-Got you!

281
00:21:57,691 --> 00:21:59,860
You're the one who texted me?

282
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:03,196
And you're the one investigating my mother

283
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:06,158
and desperately trying
to connect her to Red Dragon.

284
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:08,493
Emilia, that is not true.

285
00:22:10,037 --> 00:22:13,665
Did you know Mama
threatened me just recently?

286
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:17,669
So I won't even dare cross her.

287
00:22:19,796 --> 00:22:21,882
Now, I'm here tonight, Emilia,

288
00:22:22,174 --> 00:22:26,970
because I want to catch
the culprit myself.

289
00:22:27,262 --> 00:22:28,388
That's all it is.

290
00:22:29,473 --> 00:22:34,644
Yeah, right, Lily.
I have evidence against you.

291
00:22:44,529 --> 00:22:46,531
Well, that evidence is useless, then.

292
00:22:46,615 --> 00:22:50,452
Do you want to know why?
Because Mama will believe me.

293
00:22:50,911 --> 00:22:52,913
[chuckles] That's what you think.

294
00:22:52,996 --> 00:22:55,415
Remember, I am her daughter.

295
00:22:56,208 --> 00:23:00,003
I am the daughter your mom wishes she had.

296
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:03,715
You see, when Mama and I are together,

297
00:23:03,799 --> 00:23:04,883
time seems to fly by so fast

298
00:23:04,966 --> 00:23:06,218
because we talk about so many things.

299
00:23:06,301 --> 00:23:08,220
And your name hardly comes up
in the conversation

300
00:23:08,303 --> 00:23:10,764
because she is so disappointed in you.

301
00:23:10,847 --> 00:23:15,060
No wonder she wishes
I was her daughter instead.

302
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:17,646
-That is not true.
-Yes, it is.

303
00:23:18,980 --> 00:23:20,732
Well, Emilia?

304
00:23:21,608 --> 00:23:25,862
I bet you wish I just died
inside that flimsy coffin, huh?

305
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:27,906
I bet you wished
you never left a phone in there

306
00:23:27,989 --> 00:23:30,242
and that you actually succeeded
at killing me

307
00:23:30,325 --> 00:23:32,661
because otherwise, I wouldn't be here now.

308
00:23:32,744 --> 00:23:33,870
Well, I'm sorry.

309
00:23:34,371 --> 00:23:37,249
Wishes are all you've got now

310
00:23:37,332 --> 00:23:40,627
because I'm here in front
of you, alive and kicking.

311
00:23:41,461 --> 00:23:43,505
Do you really think, Emilia,

312
00:23:43,588 --> 00:23:46,591
that I've forgotten everything
you've done to me?

313
00:23:46,675 --> 00:23:51,721
No, Emilia, I haven't forgotten at all!

314
00:23:52,973 --> 00:23:54,891
Then again, I'm not in a rush

315
00:23:56,226 --> 00:24:00,647
because I still have to sort out
my plans for you.

316
00:24:01,439 --> 00:24:04,985
Option one: I can throw you in jail,

317
00:24:05,068 --> 00:24:08,405
but that would be too boring.

318
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:11,408
Do you want to know
what my second option is?

319
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:14,077
To bury you alive in a ditch

320
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:16,913
that you'll be digging out yourself.

321
00:24:16,997 --> 00:24:19,332
And I assure you, Emilia,

322
00:24:19,416 --> 00:24:22,419
not even Satan will be able to save you.

323
00:24:22,502 --> 00:24:24,880
[tense music intensifies]

324
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:26,965
So, you'd best not get on my bad side

325
00:24:27,716 --> 00:24:31,511
because I won't think twice
about burying you alive.

326
00:24:31,595 --> 00:24:34,431
Stop it, Lily.
Mama might get to you first.

327
00:24:34,514 --> 00:24:36,683
[laughs]

328
00:24:36,766 --> 00:24:38,894
Mama would do that? Why?

329
00:24:38,977 --> 00:24:46,067
Does she spit out fire when she gets mad?

330
00:24:46,151 --> 00:24:49,738
[suspenseful music playing]

331
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:52,532
Hey. What's the matter?

332
00:24:52,616 --> 00:24:54,951
Why can't you answer me?

333
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:58,163
Tell me, Emilia! Come on. Am I right?

334
00:24:59,122 --> 00:25:01,166
Does she spit fire when she's angry?

335
00:25:01,249 --> 00:25:04,252
Spill the beans, Emilia. Come on.

336
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:08,882
You just shut up and leave
my mother alone!

337
00:25:10,258 --> 00:25:13,470
I'll try. I'll try my best.

338
00:25:13,762 --> 00:25:17,849
But the thing is, sometimes,
there's just no stopping me.

339
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:21,269
[tense music playing]

340
00:25:21,645 --> 00:25:22,646
[exhales]

341
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:36,326
[suspenseful music playing]

342
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:47,420
Anna, Jepoy.

343
00:25:50,715 --> 00:25:53,426
You look a little happier
than usual, Arnaldo.

344
00:25:54,719 --> 00:25:59,099
Well… I think I saw an angel.

345
00:26:00,642 --> 00:26:07,065
You know, Diego's friend.
The one he was with earlier.

346
00:26:07,565 --> 00:26:11,611
I just want to ask… Is she his girlfriend?

347
00:26:12,362 --> 00:26:13,863
-[Anna] What?
-Is she my brother's girlfriend?

348
00:26:13,947 --> 00:26:14,948
[Anna] Um…

349
00:26:15,949 --> 00:26:17,075
[stutters] No.

350
00:26:18,118 --> 00:26:19,119
[quietly] She's not?

351
00:26:20,203 --> 00:26:22,706
[Anna] But… I know they're getting there.

352
00:26:23,164 --> 00:26:26,710
[unsettling music]

353
00:26:27,752 --> 00:26:30,338
She's our friend, Lily.

354
00:26:30,588 --> 00:26:31,965
[dramatic music]

355
00:26:33,258 --> 00:26:34,259
Lily.

356
00:26:34,884 --> 00:26:38,763
[tense music playing]

357
00:26:38,847 --> 00:26:39,848
[sighs]

358
00:26:49,524 --> 00:26:52,569
If she's your friend,
can you introduce me to her?

359
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:56,323
[tense music continues]

360
00:27:16,801 --> 00:27:19,679
[tense music continues]

361
00:27:36,863 --> 00:27:42,786
["Hindi Kita Iiwan" playing]

362
00:28:00,887 --> 00:28:02,972
<i>Thanks for everything, Diego.</i>

363
00:28:03,598 --> 00:28:06,226
[song continues]

364
00:28:11,064 --> 00:28:12,982
[Diego] <i>It's a bit cheesy, but I hope</i>

365
00:28:13,066 --> 00:28:15,235
<i>you feel me holding you</i>
<i>when you wear that.</i>

366
00:28:16,861 --> 00:28:23,118
<i>Wear it close to your heart</i>
<i>as a token of my undying love.</i>

367
00:28:33,002 --> 00:28:34,629
[song fades]

368
00:28:36,506 --> 00:28:39,426
[tense piano music playing]

369
00:28:57,694 --> 00:29:00,905
[tense music swells]

370
00:29:04,868 --> 00:29:05,994
[Julio] <i>Arnaldo.</i>

371
00:29:07,412 --> 00:29:08,538
<i>Who are you?</i>

372
00:29:08,621 --> 00:29:11,166
<i>Well, if you want to quit politics,</i>
<i>what do you want to do?</i>

373
00:29:11,249 --> 00:29:13,126
-<i>I want to be a priest.</i>
-[chokes]

374
00:29:13,543 --> 00:29:15,670
<i>No matter what you say,</i>
<i>I'm not going with you!</i>

375
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:19,507
<i>I was led here to fulfill</i>
<i>a mission. I can't just leave.</i>

376
00:29:19,591 --> 00:29:22,385
[henchman] <i>I'm sorry, ma'am,</i>
<i>but they ganged up on us.</i>

377
00:29:22,469 --> 00:29:24,679
<i>We weren't able to take</i>
<i>Diego Torillo with us.</i>

378
00:29:24,846 --> 00:29:28,266
[tense music continues]

379
00:29:29,893 --> 00:29:33,271
[Julio] <i>Damn you, Diego Torillo!</i>

380
00:29:33,938 --> 00:29:36,316
<i>What did you do to my grandson?!</i>

381
00:29:40,111 --> 00:29:42,530
[Lily] I tried looking for it,
Diego. I really did.

382
00:29:42,614 --> 00:29:46,201
But I couldn't find it. I'm so sorry.

383
00:29:46,743 --> 00:29:48,203
It's okay. It's just a necklace.

384
00:29:48,661 --> 00:29:51,289
Better that than me losing you.

385
00:29:51,372 --> 00:29:53,291
-It's not just a necklace.
-[chuckles softly]

386
00:29:53,374 --> 00:29:56,586
Everything you gave and did for me, Diego…

387
00:29:56,669 --> 00:29:58,296
They're all important to me.

388
00:29:58,379 --> 00:30:01,925
I don't want you to think
I'm taking all that for granted.

389
00:30:02,258 --> 00:30:04,219
They're all important to me.

390
00:30:04,302 --> 00:30:06,429
[romantic music playing]

391
00:30:06,513 --> 00:30:09,349
Lily, you don't have to prove anything.

392
00:30:10,016 --> 00:30:11,976
I know I'm important to you.

393
00:30:12,727 --> 00:30:14,437
And even if this fight goes on forever,

394
00:30:14,521 --> 00:30:18,817
I'll still be happy as long
as you're by my side.

395
00:30:20,527 --> 00:30:21,778
Don't worry about it.

396
00:30:23,404 --> 00:30:24,989
Come on. It's just a necklace.

397
00:30:28,076 --> 00:30:29,327
I'm sorry.

398
00:30:30,078 --> 00:30:31,120
It's all right.

399
00:30:32,205 --> 00:30:33,540
I'll just buy a new one.

400
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:37,126
Okay?

401
00:30:42,090 --> 00:30:45,343
[whispering] Anna, this is dangerous.

402
00:30:45,426 --> 00:30:46,427
[tense music playing]

403
00:30:46,511 --> 00:30:48,721
Lily shouldn't have come here.

404
00:30:49,722 --> 00:30:52,058
But he didn't recognize her, right?

405
00:30:52,433 --> 00:30:53,518
Yeah, for now.

406
00:30:55,019 --> 00:30:57,689
Arnaldo was crazy obsessed
with Ivy back then.

407
00:30:57,772 --> 00:31:01,067
What if his memories
come back because of her?

408
00:31:02,485 --> 00:31:05,446
Jepoy, let's just do what Lily said.

409
00:31:05,697 --> 00:31:07,699
For now, let's take care of Arnaldo.

410
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:10,660
What if the old Arnaldo comes back?

411
00:31:12,745 --> 00:31:14,122
The heartless bastard…

412
00:31:15,248 --> 00:31:16,624
who killed Nanny Carlotta.

413
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:18,209
Are we still going to protect him then?

414
00:31:22,046 --> 00:31:24,007
If that does happen, Jepoy,

415
00:31:24,090 --> 00:31:26,342
are you actually going to kill him?

416
00:31:26,926 --> 00:31:28,720
Yes. Without a doubt.

417
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:32,974
The question is…

418
00:31:38,771 --> 00:31:40,899
if Arnaldo returns to being
the devil we once knew,

419
00:31:42,025 --> 00:31:43,318
will you still protect him?

420
00:31:43,860 --> 00:31:47,780
[tense music playing]

421
00:32:17,477 --> 00:32:19,938
<i>I hope you've really changed, Arnaldo.</i>

422
00:32:20,396 --> 00:32:22,899
<i>Because if you haven't and you</i>
<i>try to hurt the ones I love,</i>

423
00:32:23,441 --> 00:32:25,443
<i>then you'll be dealing with me.</i>

424
00:32:26,235 --> 00:32:31,115
[tense music swells]

425
00:32:34,702 --> 00:32:36,371
<i>Everyone can change.</i>

426
00:32:37,330 --> 00:32:40,583
<i>Even the ones who made your life hell.</i>

427
00:32:45,254 --> 00:32:48,174
<i>I really hope I wasn't wrong</i>
<i>about you, Arnaldo.</i>

428
00:32:53,179 --> 00:32:54,764
Aren't you going to sleep yet?

429
00:32:56,516 --> 00:32:58,101
Later. You go ahead and rest.

430
00:32:59,811 --> 00:33:01,729
All right. I'll go on in.

431
00:33:07,902 --> 00:33:09,612
Jepoy, isn't that Lily?

432
00:33:09,946 --> 00:33:11,072
Where's Arnaldo?

433
00:33:11,155 --> 00:33:12,365
He's asleep.

434
00:33:13,741 --> 00:33:15,284
All right. Let's go meet Lily.

435
00:33:17,412 --> 00:33:19,080
[Lily] Jepoy, Anna.

436
00:33:19,163 --> 00:33:20,790
-[Anna] Lily, why are you here?
-Jepoy--

437
00:33:21,958 --> 00:33:23,084
I need your help.

438
00:33:25,169 --> 00:33:26,921
I need you to do something for me.

439
00:33:34,512 --> 00:33:35,972
[Diego] Lily, you have to be careful.

440
00:33:36,472 --> 00:33:38,766
We're up against
some very powerful people.

441
00:33:38,850 --> 00:33:40,101
What if they catch you?

442
00:33:40,476 --> 00:33:43,438
That won't happen, because I will reveal

443
00:33:43,521 --> 00:33:46,858
that Helena Montoya and
Red Dragon are one and the same.

444
00:33:47,859 --> 00:33:49,027
How are you going to do that?

445
00:33:49,610 --> 00:33:51,362
How will you get past her lackeys?

446
00:33:51,446 --> 00:33:53,448
I asked Jepoy for help.

447
00:33:53,531 --> 00:33:55,700
I sent him out to do something.
I planned it out.

448
00:33:58,661 --> 00:33:59,996
Just be careful.

449
00:34:03,541 --> 00:34:05,209
[tense music playing]

450
00:34:09,756 --> 00:34:11,966
[doctor] It's 120/80.

451
00:34:12,050 --> 00:34:14,093
-Your blood pressure is normal.
-[Julio scoffs]

452
00:34:14,177 --> 00:34:16,804
Just continue taking your medicine

453
00:34:16,888 --> 00:34:18,347
and getting plenty of rest,

454
00:34:18,431 --> 00:34:20,475
and you'll be back to your old self.

455
00:34:21,934 --> 00:34:26,564
Doc, I've already told you
that my condition

456
00:34:26,647 --> 00:34:28,232
will only get worse

457
00:34:28,316 --> 00:34:31,736
as long as my grandson
stays the way he is now.

458
00:34:32,737 --> 00:34:36,532
What I need you to do
is to bring back Arnaldo.

459
00:34:36,616 --> 00:34:40,953
I mean, bring my grandson
back to how he was.

460
00:34:41,037 --> 00:34:43,539
The Arnaldo I know. Not this…

461
00:34:43,623 --> 00:34:47,502
Not this goody-two-shoes wannabe
who gives me a migraine.

462
00:34:47,585 --> 00:34:49,712
There are alternative
treatments, Governor.

463
00:34:50,171 --> 00:34:52,632
Unconventional, but effective
in some cases.

464
00:34:53,007 --> 00:34:55,051
We can use hypnosis,

465
00:34:55,134 --> 00:34:57,637
or maybe acupuncture to treat the patient.

466
00:34:57,720 --> 00:35:02,809
How can you do that when
my grandson isn't even here?

467
00:35:04,018 --> 00:35:07,772
Sometimes, you just need to
jump-start the patient's brain.

468
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:14,362
By that, I mean images that'll
ignite an intense emotion.

469
00:35:21,536 --> 00:35:22,537
[Jepoy] Thanks.

470
00:35:25,081 --> 00:35:26,082
Lily.

471
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:33,506
I've done what you asked me to.

472
00:35:37,385 --> 00:35:39,470
This is a clone of Mercedes' phone.

473
00:35:40,096 --> 00:35:42,974
You can keep track of all her calls

474
00:35:43,057 --> 00:35:44,225
and text messages from here.

475
00:35:50,273 --> 00:35:51,524
Thank you, Jepoy.

476
00:35:52,859 --> 00:35:54,485
I can always count on you.

477
00:36:02,910 --> 00:36:04,120
-[Pandoy] One for you.
-[Loring] Hmm.

478
00:36:04,203 --> 00:36:05,121
-There.
-Here we go.

479
00:36:05,204 --> 00:36:07,874
-One for Diego. One for me.
-[Loring chuckles]

480
00:36:07,957 --> 00:36:09,125
-Nanny, Uncle.
-[Loring] Come and join us.

481
00:36:09,208 --> 00:36:12,086
-Diego, you're just in time.
-That looks really good!

482
00:36:12,170 --> 00:36:14,964
Of course. I prepared
all of your favorites.

483
00:36:15,047 --> 00:36:17,175
-[Pandoy] Right.
-Yummy, right?

484
00:36:17,258 --> 00:36:18,885
It's not my birthday we're celebrating.

485
00:36:18,968 --> 00:36:19,969
[Pandoy] Hey.

486
00:36:20,052 --> 00:36:22,847
She's been thinking of what
to prepare since last week.

487
00:36:22,930 --> 00:36:24,515
-[Loring] That's true.
-[Pandoy chuckles]

488
00:36:24,599 --> 00:36:26,392
This is why I love you so much, Nanny.

489
00:36:28,477 --> 00:36:30,188
-[Diego] Besides, Uncle…
-Yes?

490
00:36:30,271 --> 00:36:32,899
Our birthday only comes once a year,

491
00:36:32,982 --> 00:36:35,401
so we have to celebrate.

492
00:36:35,484 --> 00:36:40,114
Well, I hope Lily can come
to my birthday tomorrow.

493
00:36:40,740 --> 00:36:44,702
That reminds me, where's Lily?
Has she found Red Dragon?

494
00:36:45,912 --> 00:36:47,580
That's what she's doing right now.

495
00:36:48,331 --> 00:36:50,958
She cloned the phone
of Red Dragon's secretary

496
00:36:51,042 --> 00:36:53,252
to keep tabs on everything they do.

497
00:36:55,922 --> 00:36:57,048
You can do that?

498
00:36:57,131 --> 00:36:58,090
How?

499
00:36:59,175 --> 00:37:01,886
-Cloning…
-Oh, whatever.

500
00:37:01,969 --> 00:37:03,804
At least we know Lily's doing something.

501
00:37:03,888 --> 00:37:05,681
-Right. Let's just eat.
-Yes. This is what's important.

502
00:37:05,765 --> 00:37:06,849
-You have to try this.
-That's right.

503
00:37:06,933 --> 00:37:08,976
-I made your favorites.
-Looks like I'm gonna eat a lot, Nanny.

504
00:37:09,060 --> 00:37:10,061
-Yes!
-I know.

505
00:37:10,561 --> 00:37:13,940
[tense music playing]

506
00:37:18,152 --> 00:37:22,907
[ringing]

507
00:37:29,497 --> 00:37:30,289
[Mercedes] <i>Madam?</i>

508
00:37:30,373 --> 00:37:33,084
I've already settled my problem
with Mr. Yi…

509
00:37:33,167 --> 00:37:36,045
<i>…regarding the gun shipment.</i>

510
00:37:37,213 --> 00:37:39,924
What about the guns
in the possession of the police?

511
00:37:40,007 --> 00:37:41,884
I've already dealt with that.

512
00:37:42,176 --> 00:37:44,220
[Red Dragon] <i>They won't be able</i>
<i>to trace them to me.</i>

513
00:37:45,554 --> 00:37:47,348
[Mercedes] <i>I have one other</i>
<i>concern, Madam.</i>

514
00:37:47,431 --> 00:37:50,643
Emilia says she wants
to get rid of someone.

515
00:37:51,852 --> 00:37:53,854
[Red Dragon] <i>Prioritize the shipment.</i>

516
00:37:54,230 --> 00:37:56,357
And I will take care of my daughter.

517
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:57,733
Yes.

518
00:37:59,235 --> 00:38:04,699
[tense music swells]

519
00:38:10,830 --> 00:38:12,123
It's confirmed.

520
00:38:12,206 --> 00:38:17,920
That's another piece of evidence proving
that Helena Montoya is Red Dragon.

521
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:22,258
But with all of the supposed
good things she has done,

522
00:38:23,092 --> 00:38:26,595
the people of Poblacion Ardiente
now see her as an angel.

523
00:38:28,848 --> 00:38:32,435
Let's see if they'll still
see her as an angel

524
00:38:32,768 --> 00:38:34,937
once I expose all of her crimes.

525
00:38:35,855 --> 00:38:42,153
I'll gather more evidence to
prove to the people of Ardiente

526
00:38:42,236 --> 00:38:45,448
just who the real Helena Montoya is.

527
00:38:47,533 --> 00:38:49,869
The people of Poblacion Ardiente
will soon learn

528
00:38:49,952 --> 00:38:56,459
that their supposed angel
is actually a devil in disguise.

529
00:39:03,966 --> 00:39:06,427
"And he was so surprised to see the turtle

530
00:39:06,510 --> 00:39:08,929
standing on the top of the mountain

531
00:39:09,013 --> 00:39:10,598
because he knew he had lost the race.

532
00:39:10,973 --> 00:39:13,225
All the rabbit could do was cry."

533
00:39:14,352 --> 00:39:16,645
Well, kids? Did you like our story today?

534
00:39:16,729 --> 00:39:18,606
We did!

535
00:39:18,689 --> 00:39:21,859
All right, we'll finish the rest
of the stories tomorrow.

536
00:39:21,942 --> 00:39:25,738
You have to go home now.
It's getting late.

537
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:28,908
[kid 1] Teacher Anna, Teacher Anna,
can you go with us?

538
00:39:28,991 --> 00:39:32,953
Of course. I can walk with you
to the entrance. Shall we go?

539
00:39:33,037 --> 00:39:35,247
-[children] Yes, ma'am!
-Okay.

540
00:39:35,748 --> 00:39:37,124
[Anna] Come on. Let's go.

541
00:39:39,085 --> 00:39:40,419
Careful.

542
00:39:44,465 --> 00:39:46,801
You go with them, Anna.
I'll clean up here.

543
00:39:50,554 --> 00:39:51,806
Jepoy.

544
00:39:54,725 --> 00:39:56,435
Go on. I won't do anything to him.

545
00:39:57,728 --> 00:39:59,146
Remember what I told you.

546
00:40:02,900 --> 00:40:04,026
[Anna] Let's go.

547
00:40:11,075 --> 00:40:13,536
There. [chuckles]

548
00:40:15,663 --> 00:40:19,708
[tense music playing]

549
00:40:24,171 --> 00:40:26,924
Here. One, two, three.

550
00:40:27,007 --> 00:40:28,884
[Jepoy] <i>What if the old Arnaldo</i>
<i>comes back?</i>

551
00:40:28,968 --> 00:40:31,262
<i>Are you actually going to kill him?</i>

552
00:40:31,345 --> 00:40:33,180
<i>Without a doubt.</i>

553
00:40:37,351 --> 00:40:38,352
Wow.

554
00:40:42,398 --> 00:40:44,608
My friend fish swim pretty fast.

555
00:40:55,578 --> 00:40:59,415
[suspenseful music playing]

556
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:01,750
[door opens]

557
00:41:15,931 --> 00:41:18,225
[Julio] <i>Every corner of Poblacion Ardiente</i>

558
00:41:18,309 --> 00:41:21,353
<i>is etched in my mind.</i>

559
00:41:21,437 --> 00:41:22,771
<i>But it's not the same for you,</i>

560
00:41:22,855 --> 00:41:23,939
<i>that's why you have to study this.</i>

561
00:41:24,023 --> 00:41:26,984
<i>Until you can control every piece of it</i>

562
00:41:27,067 --> 00:41:28,569
<i>from wherever you are.</i>

563
00:41:28,652 --> 00:41:32,072
<i>That is the mark of a true leader.</i>

564
00:41:32,156 --> 00:41:35,784
<i>Arnaldo, you are the man.</i>

565
00:41:35,868 --> 00:41:38,037
<i>Who else would I take after?</i>
<i>I learned from the best.</i>

566
00:41:38,120 --> 00:41:39,914
<i>-Cheers!</i>
<i>-Cheers!</i>

567
00:41:39,997 --> 00:41:43,417
-[Julio] <i>To Mayor Arnaldo!</i>
-[Arnaldo] <i>Like you said.</i>

568
00:41:43,501 --> 00:41:45,294
[Arnaldo] <i>Failure is not an option.</i>

569
00:41:45,377 --> 00:41:50,007
[Julio] <i>You'll be running</i>
<i>for senator in my place.</i>

570
00:41:50,257 --> 00:41:55,054
[Julio] <i>You need Miss Aguas</i>
<i>for your candidacy.</i>

571
00:41:57,389 --> 00:41:59,683
[doctor] <i>Sometimes, you</i>
<i>just need to jump start</i>

572
00:41:59,767 --> 00:42:01,352
<i>the patient's brain.</i>

573
00:42:02,561 --> 00:42:07,691
<i>By that, I mean images that'll</i>
<i>ignite an intense emotion.</i>

574
00:42:08,943 --> 00:42:11,529
[tense music continues]

575
00:42:15,282 --> 00:42:18,786
[Julio] <i>I'm sure Ivy can sponsor</i>
<i>this event for you.</i>

576
00:42:18,869 --> 00:42:20,371
<i>If it's okay,</i>
<i>I'd rather leave Ivy out of this.</i>

577
00:42:20,454 --> 00:42:21,872
<i>I don't want her to think</i>

578
00:42:21,956 --> 00:42:24,667
<i>that we're only after her money</i>
<i>or that we're just using her.</i>

579
00:42:24,750 --> 00:42:26,335
<i>But it's the truth, right?</i>

580
00:42:26,418 --> 00:42:29,338
<i>Actually, no. Not anymore.</i>
<i>I'm already in love with her.</i>

581
00:42:29,630 --> 00:42:31,048
[Julio] <i>What's going on with you?</i>

582
00:42:31,131 --> 00:42:33,968
<i>You're so obsessed with Miss Aguas.</i>

583
00:42:34,051 --> 00:42:35,386
-[Julio] <i>You can't even think…</i>
-[Lily] <i>You monster!</i>

584
00:42:35,469 --> 00:42:36,720
-<i>…straight anymore.</i>
-[Arnaldo] <i>I didn't mean to!</i>

585
00:42:36,804 --> 00:42:38,097
<i>You bastard!</i>

586
00:42:39,056 --> 00:42:40,182
<i>Arnaldo, get up!</i>

587
00:42:40,266 --> 00:42:42,351
[Arnaldo] <i>Don't touch me!</i>
<i>Stay out of this!</i>

588
00:42:43,602 --> 00:42:47,856
[Julio] <i>Arnaldo. You were the</i>
<i>golden boy of our family.</i>

589
00:42:47,940 --> 00:42:51,819
<i>How could you let that woman</i>
<i>ruin your life?!</i>

590
00:42:51,902 --> 00:42:55,447
<i>I! V! Y!</i>

591
00:42:55,531 --> 00:42:58,909
-[Julio] <i>Damn you, Ivy Aguas!</i>
-[Arnaldo shouting]

592
00:42:58,993 --> 00:43:01,954
[Julio] <i>What have you done to my grandson?</i>

593
00:43:03,289 --> 00:43:08,502
<i>I'm not done with you, Ivy.</i>
<i>I am not yet done with you!</i>

594
00:43:10,546 --> 00:43:14,967
[tense music swells]

595
00:43:17,636 --> 00:43:20,306
<i>I'll get you back, Arnaldo.</i>

596
00:43:20,973 --> 00:43:26,270
<i>You'll be the man you once were.</i>
<i>I promise you that.</i>

597
00:43:47,249 --> 00:43:50,502
[suspenseful music playing]

598
00:44:02,431 --> 00:44:04,058
Gee, you're fast!

599
00:44:04,683 --> 00:44:07,603
But just you wait! I'll catch you!

600
00:44:08,312 --> 00:44:09,313
There!

601
00:44:10,147 --> 00:44:11,398
Man, this is hard.

602
00:44:13,317 --> 00:44:14,985
Can't you guys just stay still?

603
00:44:21,909 --> 00:44:25,579
[suspenseful music continues]

604
00:44:37,716 --> 00:44:41,303
Hang on, Arnaldo,
you're not doing it right.

605
00:44:43,597 --> 00:44:44,640
What am I doing wrong?

606
00:44:44,723 --> 00:44:46,266
That's not how you catch catfish.

607
00:45:02,116 --> 00:45:03,867
-[Jepoy] See?
-Where is it? Can I see?

608
00:45:04,743 --> 00:45:06,328
[laughs]

609
00:45:08,205 --> 00:45:10,958
You're all talk.
You didn't even catch one.

610
00:45:11,458 --> 00:45:13,669
Fine. Your turn. Go on.

611
00:45:15,462 --> 00:45:19,842
Let's see now. There. Hold on.

612
00:45:29,893 --> 00:45:35,190
[suspenseful music swells]

613
00:45:43,615 --> 00:45:44,616
Jepoy!

614
00:45:49,413 --> 00:45:50,956
Anna, look. I caught one.

615
00:45:52,040 --> 00:45:55,169
-[Jepoy] You did it. Nice!
-[Arnaldo and Jepoy chuckle]

616
00:45:55,252 --> 00:45:56,587
[Arnaldo] So that's the trick!

617
00:45:56,670 --> 00:45:58,213
Jepoy taught me how to catch catfish.

618
00:46:01,925 --> 00:46:03,177
This one's huge!

619
00:46:05,429 --> 00:46:07,723
-Pretty easy, right?
-Yeah. I get it now.

620
00:46:07,806 --> 00:46:10,309
From now on, I'll do it
the way you taught me.

621
00:46:10,392 --> 00:46:12,811
We sure caught a big one,
just enough for our dinner.

622
00:46:12,895 --> 00:46:14,480
Do you know how to cook it?

623
00:46:14,563 --> 00:46:18,984
The problem is that I still have to
gather firewood before cooking.

624
00:46:19,067 --> 00:46:21,487
I'm not good at cooking,
but I'll figure it out soon.

625
00:46:21,570 --> 00:46:23,030
I'm sure you'll get the hang of it.

626
00:46:33,665 --> 00:46:35,334
[Arnaldo] Perfect. We caught three.

627
00:46:35,417 --> 00:46:37,044
It goes really well with…

628
00:46:38,545 --> 00:46:39,671
Arnaldo.

629
00:46:40,797 --> 00:46:45,552
[tense music playing]

630
00:47:03,529 --> 00:47:05,948
[Helena] <i>You know,</i>
<i>when your phone blacks out,</i>

631
00:47:06,031 --> 00:47:08,408
<i>it means it's been cloned.</i>

632
00:47:08,492 --> 00:47:09,952
<i>-That's impossible, Madam.</i>
<i>-Shut up!</i>

633
00:47:10,035 --> 00:47:12,746
[Lily] <i>I'm sure Red Dragon already knows</i>

634
00:47:12,829 --> 00:47:14,122
<i>that I'm her enemy.</i>

635
00:47:14,206 --> 00:47:16,083
[Arnaldo] <i>I've been having</i>
<i>some thoughts lately.</i>

636
00:47:16,166 --> 00:47:17,000
<i>About a woman.</i>

637
00:47:17,084 --> 00:47:19,294
-[Diego] <i>Well, what do you see?</i>
-[Arnaldo] <i>Uncontrollable lust.</i>

638
00:47:20,128 --> 00:47:22,631
[Diego] <i>Don't you dare come</i>
<i>near my brother again.</i>

639
00:47:22,714 --> 00:47:27,052
<i>I want you to kill Diego Torillo now!</i>

640
00:47:27,135 --> 00:47:30,597
[Helena] <i>I just realized</i>
<i>that I'm allergic to flowers.</i>

641
00:47:30,681 --> 00:47:32,558
<i>Lilies in particular.</i>

642
00:47:32,641 --> 00:47:35,102
[Emilia] <i>I will watch how the queen works.</i>

643
00:47:35,185 --> 00:47:36,228
[Helena] <i>Exactly.</i>

644
00:47:36,311 --> 00:47:39,314
[theme music playing]
